  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the maximum loss in each lottery — specifically, it prefers the lottery with the smaller maximum loss. In this case, A has a maximum loss of 0, B has a maximum loss of 2400, so A is preferred. However, the individual’s verbal report does not mention maximum loss or any evaluation of losses. Instead, the individual evaluates the risk of not getting any gain (i.e., zero outcome) and values the certainty of A. This reflects a different reasoning — one based on avoiding zero outcomes and valuing certainty — rather than a focus on the magnitude of potential losses. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason about maximum loss being more favorable. The information considered (risk of zero gain) is not equivalent to the information required by the decision reason (maximum loss), and the justification (avoiding risk of no gain) does not match the rule of preferring the lottery with the more favorable maximum loss. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
